#Task 3

##File Permissions

## File creating shell file
echo "Hello World" > HelloWorld.sh

## Make it executable
chmod +x HelloWorld.sh
## Change ownership
sudo chown root:root HelloWorld.sh

## Understanding permissions
ls -l HelloWorld.sh
## Ouput:
-rwxr-xr-x 1 root   root     12 Sep 17 22:44  HelloWorld.sh
## Breakdown: owner(rwx) group(r-x) others(r-x)
## Challenge: Create a file that only you can read/write, but others can only read. Document the command.

## create file
touch file.txt

## change Permission of file
chmod 644 file.txt
## check 
ls -l file.txt
## Output: -rw-r--r-- 1 jtshab jtshab    0 Sep 17 22:52  file.txt
## Breakdown: owner(rw-) group(r--) others(r--)
